**Event Load: LIGHT** — calibrated to ~1,900 words (slightly over the LIGHT band, because the watchlist and sector sections carry real signal even on an empty-calendar day).

Key calls in the brief:

- **Calendar is nearly empty.** Only item is Bessent speaking at 14:00 ET, Actual = "—", written as *Scheduled, not yet occurred*. No economic releases. The Jackson Hole / PCE / FOMC-minutes material lives only in the RSS feed analysis, so I labeled it feed-sourced rather than calendar-confirmed.
- **No watchlist earnings today.** NVDA and CRWD both land Wednesday 8/26 — that's the week's real event, with PANW/AVGO/ZS clustered 9/1–9/3.
- **The selling is localized, not broad.** Nasdaq futures -0.61% vs S&P -0.22%; seven of ten movers are watchlist names and five are the memory/optical complex (MU, MRVL, GLW, CIEN all -3%+, AAOI -12%). Europe flatly declined to follow Asia's Kospi -3.12% memory-led drop.
- **No Tier 1 name moved more than 3%** — all >3% damage sits in Tier 2/3. Flagged RSI extremes both ways: SQM 73 / FCX 69 / ALB 68 stretched, HON 33 / FLNC 35 / AVGO 39 washed out, with AVGO sitting below its 200-day into a 9/2 report.

Two data issues I surfaced rather than smoothed over: the snapshot was collected at **11:39 PT** yet is labeled pre-market, and S&P futures and "previous close" both print 7,674 with all US indices at +0.00% — so I told the reader to trust the change columns, not the index levels. FRED timed out (2Y is a prev-close carry), Stooq 404'd all three calls, Schwab errored on 6 of 362.
